<p>Another month, another <a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell">agent-shell</a> update. If you missed the last post, have a look at the <a href="https://xenodium.com/agent-shell-0-87-updates">0.87 update</a>. This time around, the most notable changes are around rendering, performance, and bugfixes, sprinkled with new features here and there.</p>
<p>As usual, this post showcases highlights, but please check out the <a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/compare/v0.87.4...v0.98.2">full list of changes</a> if you're after the nitty-gritty.</p>
<h2>What's <code>agent-shell</code>?</h2>
<p><a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell">agent-shell</a> brings your favorite AI agents to <a href="https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/">Emacs</a>, keeping you at home: familiar buffers and bindings, no terminal emulation. All powered by ACP, the <a href="https://agentclientprotocol.com/">Agent Client Protocol</a>.</p>
<h2>New supported agent</h2>
<p><a href="https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness">DeepSeek Harness</a> joins the family, bringing the total number of supported agents to 24. Start DeepSeek with <code>M-x agent-shell-deepseek-start-agent</code>, or pick it from <code>M-x agent-shell</code> as usual.</p>
<h2>Antigravity moved to <code>agy</code> (action required)</h2>
<p>Latest Antigravity ships with ACP out of the box, so <code>agent-shell</code> now runs <code>agy acp</code> rather than a separate binary you had to download and unpack. If you're an Antigravity user, install a recent CLI, make sure <code>agy</code> is on your <code>PATH</code>, and sign in once:</p>
<pre><code class="language-{.bash">agy acp --login
</code></pre>
<h2>Blockquotes: rendering + navigation + copy</h2>
<p>Blockquotes improved their display, rendering embedded Markdown (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/issues/942">#942</a>).</p>
<p><img src="https://xenodium.github.io/images/agent-shell-0-98-updates/blockquotes-markdown.png" alt=""></p>
<p>They also joined the TAB navigation party. <code>TAB</code> and <code>S-TAB</code> now visit blockquotes, stopping on their first quoted character.</p>
<p><img src="https://xenodium.github.io/images/agent-shell-0-98-updates/blockquotes-tab.gif" alt=""></p>
<p>With point on a blockquote, <code>RET</code> now copies the quote's raw Markdown, without the <code>&gt;</code> markers.</p>
<p><img src="https://xenodium.github.io/images/agent-shell-0-98-updates/blockquotes-copy.gif" alt=""></p>
<h2>Images in table cells</h2>
<p>Images are now rendered as thumbnails within tables. Press <code>RET</code> on an image to open in full view.</p>
<p><img src="https://xenodium.github.io/images/agent-shell-0-98-updates/images-table.gif" alt=""></p>
<p>Thank you <a href="https://github.com/alberti42">@alberti42</a> for <a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/938">#938</a>. Tables also realign in the resized window's own buffer now (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/issues/934">#934</a>), so splitting a window no longer leaves a table laid out for the window it used to be in.</p>
<h2>Links</h2>
<p>Hovering a rendered link (or with point on one) now shows its target URL, so you can judge whether it's worth opening.</p>
<p>Two new entry points landed alongside (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/issues/933">#933</a>):</p>
<ul>
<li><code>agent-shell-markdown-open-link-at-point</code> opens the link at point.</li>
<li><code>agent-shell-markdown-xref-backend</code> plugs into <code>xref-backend-functions</code>, so <code>M-.</code> on a rendered <code>path:line</code> citation visits it. It returns nil anywhere else, web and binary links included, leaving point to the next backend.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Recursive folding</h2>
<p><code>RET</code> toggles the fragment at point, as usual. <code>C-u RET</code> now toggles groups recursively (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/issues/924">#924</a>, <a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/issues/945">#945</a>).</p>
<h2>Queued -&gt; steered</h2>
<p>Queued a prompt, but wanted to steer instead? Pressing <code>M-RET</code> on an empty prompt now offers to steer the last queued prompt into the running turn (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/issues/918">#918</a>, <a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/issues/919">#919</a>). While this isn't something I need often, I'm pretty happy with the UX we landed on.</p>
<p>While on the topic of steering, chat mode now handles steered prompt labelling (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/930">#930</a>, proposed by <a href="https://github.com/Gleek">@Gleek</a>). If you'd like to render labels differently, <code>agent-shell-chat-label-function</code> now receives the <code>:steered</code> param.</p>
<h2>Exposing more options in header</h2>
<p>Agents often expose options that never make it to the buffer header. Additional options are now offered via the <code>(+N)</code> menu (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/issues/921">#921</a>).</p>
<h2>Filtering noisy notices</h2>
<p>Agents write all sorts to stderr, and <code>agent-shell</code> surfaces it under &quot;Notices&quot;. You can now use <code>agent-shell-notice-filter-function</code> to filter notices (or modify) as preferred (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/issues/950">#950</a> by <a href="https://github.com/astoff">@astoff</a>). It receives an alist with <code>:text</code>, one stderr line, and returns the text to show or nil to drop it:</p>
<pre><code class="language-{.commonlisp">(setopt agent-shell-notice-filter-function
        (lambda (notice)
          (unless (string-prefix-p &quot;[idle-compaction]&quot; (map-elt notice :text))
            (map-elt notice :text))))
</code></pre>
<p>A filter that signals or returns a non-string is reported, and the notice shown unfiltered.</p>
<h2>Your own system prompt</h2>
<p><code>agent-shell-system-prompt</code> is appended to the agent's default system prompt, sent whenever a session is created, loaded, resumed or forked (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/acp.el/issues/37">acp.el #37</a> by <a href="https://github.com/systemfreund">@systemfreund</a>):</p>
<pre><code class="language-{.commonlisp">(setopt agent-shell-system-prompt &quot;Keep answers short and respond like a pirate.&quot;)
</code></pre>
<p>Only agents advertising ACP's <code>systemPrompt</code> capability can take one. Configure a prompt for an agent that can't, and <code>agent-shell</code> says it's ignored rather than dropping it quietly. An agent config's <code>:system-prompt</code> takes precedence.</p>
<h2>Secrets resolved at agent start</h2>
<p><code>agent-shell-make-environment-variables</code> now takes a function as a value and calls it when the agent starts, rather than when your config loads (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/issues/948">#948</a> by <a href="https://github.com/nbarrientos">@nbarrientos</a>). Handy for a password store still locked at init:</p>
<pre><code class="language-{.commonlisp">(setopt agent-shell-opencode-environment
        (agent-shell-make-environment-variables
         &quot;MY_SECRET&quot; (lambda ()
                       (auth-source-pick-first-password :host &quot;example.org&quot;))))
</code></pre>
<p>A function that errors or returns nil leaves the variable out of the agent's environment and says so in a boxed warning in the shell. Works across all agents.</p>
<h2>Shells follow <code>project-switch-project</code></h2>
<p>Starting a shell from <code>C-x p p</code> used to land in the current shell's directory rather than the project you just picked, and offer that directory's sessions to resume. It now starts in the chosen project (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/949">#949</a> by <a href="https://github.com/OSadovy">@OSadovy</a>).</p>
<h2>Fork and show history</h2>
<p>When <code>agent-shell-session-fork-restore-history</code> is non-nil, forked sessions will attempt to restore interaction history as per <code>agent-shell-session-restore-verbosity</code>.</p>
<p><code>agent-shell-session-fork-restore-history</code> is off by default, so you'll need to enable it with:</p>
<pre><code class="language-{.commonlisp">(setopt agent-shell-session-fork-restore-history t)
</code></pre>
<p>Note: You'll need an agent that supports loading a session right after forking it, like <code>claude-agent-acp 0.90.0</code> or newer.</p>
<h2>Faster streaming</h2>
<p>Streaming performance received some love. Message chunks are coalesced before rendering (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/883">#883</a> by <a href="https://github.com/moyotar">@moyotar</a>), thought chunks are batched the same way, and restored sessions replay with far less overhead (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/897">#897</a> by <a href="https://github.com/Gleek">@Gleek</a>).</p>
<h2>Lots of fixes</h2>
<p>As mentioned, the much effort in the release went into fixes and improvements.</p>
<p>Rendering:</p>
<ul>
<li>Bold renders next to text and punctuation (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/925">#925</a> by <a href="https://github.com/vritser">@vritser</a>), with CommonMark flanking rules relaxed for CJK (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/issues/942">#942</a>).</li>
<li>Numbered headers and bold steps no longer render as list items (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/939">#939</a> by <a href="https://github.com/budu">@budu</a>), nor does markup that merely reads like one.</li>
<li>A fenced block's last line is fontified (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/916">#916</a> by <a href="https://github.com/liaowang11">@liaowang11</a>), two flush source blocks render as two (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/issues/940">#940</a>), and nested ones stay verbatim while streaming.</li>
<li>Headers keep their title when a code fence follows directly (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/issues/947">#947</a>).</li>
<li>Text quoted into the prompt keeps its quote face (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/952">#952</a> by <a href="https://github.com/OSadovy">@OSadovy</a>).</li>
<li>Copilot multi-hunk diffs render as separate hunks (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/issues/931">#931</a>), and Codex streamed output is fenced correctly (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/906">#906</a> by <a href="https://github.com/bartbunting">@bartbunting</a>).</li>
<li>Icons scale correctly on HiDPI Linux (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/917">#917</a> by <a href="https://github.com/heraplem">@heraplem</a>).</li>
<li>Unfinished tool calls survive turn end (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/issues/941">#941</a>), so a late subagent keeps its title and grouping.</li>
</ul>
<p>Performance and responsiveness:</p>
<ul>
<li>Buffers shown in no window measure against a live one (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/885">#885</a> by <a href="https://github.com/bcc32">@bcc32</a>), and measuring glyph height no longer triggers window hooks (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/886">#886</a>, also <a href="https://github.com/bcc32">@bcc32</a>).</li>
<li><code>agent-shell-cwd-function</code> is called once per command (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/857">#857</a>, also <a href="https://github.com/bcc32">@bcc32</a>).</li>
<li>Pending Markdown is protected and fontification updates silenced (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/915">#915</a> by <a href="https://github.com/daym">@daym</a>).</li>
<li>Chat mode relabels only the last turn while streaming, not the whole buffer (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/943">#943</a>, profiled and proposed by <a href="https://github.com/Gleek">@Gleek</a>).</li>
<li>In <a href="https://github.com/xenodium/shell-maker">shell-maker</a>, auto-scroll can be suppressed during bulk updates (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/shell-maker/pull/50">#50</a> by <a href="https://github.com/Gleek">@Gleek</a>), which is what makes the faster replay possible.</li>
<li>Also in shell-maker, the <code>curl --version</code> check that ran on every submission is gone (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/shell-maker/issues/32">#32</a> by <a href="https://github.com/carlosdagos">@carlosdagos</a>).</li>
<li>In <a href="https://github.com/xenodium/acp.el">acp.el</a>, agents handle <code>SIGTERM</code> before being killed on shutdown (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/acp.el/pull/35">#35</a> by <a href="https://github.com/fjolliton">@fjolliton</a>).</li>
</ul>
<p>Elsewhere:</p>
<ul>
<li>Undo history no longer carries programmatic renders: the compose buffer starts empty (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/893">#893</a> by <a href="https://github.com/liaowang11">@liaowang11</a>) and resets after a deferred render (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/902">#902</a> by <a href="https://github.com/bcc32">@bcc32</a>).</li>
<li>New worktrees stay under the main working tree (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/904">#904</a> by <a href="https://github.com/xiaofeilovecoding">@xiaofeilovecoding</a>).</li>
<li>A restored session finishes initializing even when rendering errors (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/887">#887</a> by <a href="https://github.com/bcc32">@bcc32</a>).</li>
<li>Flymake context is only used when <code>flymake-mode</code> is on (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/892">#892</a> by <a href="https://github.com/liaowang11">@liaowang11</a>), and single-line regions carry one line number (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/922">#922</a> by <a href="https://github.com/martenlienen">@martenlienen</a>).</li>
<li>Quoting a region leaves the mark where reading stopped (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/896">#896</a> by <a href="https://github.com/OSadovy">@OSadovy</a>).</li>
<li>Minibuffer completion keeps the agent's candidate order (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/929">#929</a> by <a href="https://github.com/Zzull">@Zzull</a>).</li>
<li>Remote URLs are skipped when parsing local links (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/926">#926</a> by <a href="https://github.com/mpmiszczyk">@mpmiszczyk</a>), and optional system-sleep functions are declared (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/pull/928">#928</a> by <a href="https://github.com/mboldt">@mboldt</a>).</li>
<li>In shell-maker, non-ASCII prompt history no longer reads back as raw bytes, and entries already corrupted by older versions are decoded on read (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/shell-maker/issues/49">#49</a> by <a href="https://github.com/kazmuroi">@kazmuroi</a>).</li>
<li>In <a href="https://github.com/xenodium/acp.el">acp.el</a>, agent stderr reaches error handlers one line at a time rather than in arbitrary pipe chunks (added for notice filtering).</li>
</ul>
<h2>Public functions</h2>
<p>A few more additions for package authors building on <code>agent-shell</code>.</p>
<h3>Prompt locations</h3>
<p><code>agent-shell-prompt-ranges</code> returns the range of every prompt in the buffer, in buffer order, covering prompts typed at the shell, replayed by a restored session, and steered into a running turn (<a href="https://github.com/xenodium/agent-shell/issues/882">#882</a>). Each comes back as an alist spanning the comint shell prompt itself (<code>:prompt-start</code>, <code>:prompt-end</code>) and the input typed after it (<code>:input-start</code>, <code>:input-end</code>).</p>
<h3>Usage events and ACP <code>_meta</code></h3>
<p><code>agent-shell-subscribe-to</code> now offers a <code>usage-update</code> event, broadcast when the agent reports context window or cost usage. Events now also carry ACP's <code>_meta</code>, so integrations can read whatever an agent attaches without waiting on <code>agent-shell</code>.</p>
<h3>Choosing sessions programmatically</h3>
<p><code>agent-shell-session-strategy</code> now accepts a function. It's called with the resumeable sessions and returns <code>new</code>, <code>latest</code>, <code>prompt</code>, or a <code>(session-id . ID)</code> cons to load a specific one:</p>
<pre><code class="language-{.commonlisp">(setopt agent-shell-session-strategy
        (lambda (context)
          (if (map-elt context :sessions) 'latest 'new)))
</code></pre>
